<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Darini</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of north-east Ireland recorded by Ptolemy, sometimes linked with the Dáirine of early Irish genealogies.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150 lists the Darini in north-east Ireland, inland or on the coast between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/robogdii">Robogdii</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/voluntii">Voluntii</a>, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-antrim">County Antrim</a> or north Down. Like his other Irish names, this information came from earlier seafarers' reports and is hard to locate precisely.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers or society from classical sources. Some scholars connect the name with the Dáirine, descendants of a legendary ancestor Dáire, a grouping that in Irish tradition includes the ruling families of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/iverni">Érainn</a> and of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dal-fiatach">Dal Fiatach</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-ireland">Ulster</a>, though the link is uncertain.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Darini disappear from the written record after Ptolemy. Their region later lay within the territories of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ulaid">Kingdom of Ulaid</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dal-naraidi">Dal nAraidi</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/darini.jpg" alt="Darini" width="320" height="407"><figcaption>Image: Paul S · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy_ire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=darini" aria-label="Darini on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4621 330 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Darini lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4941 586h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4941 586h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=darini">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

